  "style": {
    "name": "Flamboyant Gothic reliquary-facade",
    "rationale": "Second pass: the first build had a strong amber-and-blue massing but no real rose, a shallow portal, and broad flat fields. I added the great stepped concentric rose medallion with gold tracery ribs above a true 3-block-deep pointed gold-edged portal; framed the central bay with projecting pilasters and three gold string-courses; deepened relief by breaking every plane wider than six with chiseled panels, lancet slits, quoined turret edges and crocketed rakes; engaged the blue-terracotta spires and gable directly onto the body (no sky between); and held the document's warm split-complementary palette — red-sandstone body, saturated blue-terracotta roofs, gold accents and blue/red jewel-glass — against the reference's pale stone rather than copying it."
  },
